customs tariff of China as notified to the WTO IDB for 2025; WTO Integrated Database (IDB), applied tariff notified by China for 2025 (HS 2022), read on the WTO Tariff & Trade Data browse pages (ttd.wto.org/en/data/idb/applied-duties?member=C156&product=<line>&year=2025, retrieved 2026-11-21; customs/packs/cn.json)

* CN: 52 tariff lines and 1 preference groups from the member's IDB notification for 2025; each preference group gives a partner its lowest notified rate per line (the kernel takes the first preference listing the origin)
* origin not given: MFN (the model's convention, `mfnIfOriginUnknown`)
* grade B: official intergovernmental data (WTO IDB, notified by the member); the national tariff instrument is not read

Not modelled (grade C or noted):
* only the HS subheadings of customs/HS_MAP.md are modelled (any other code: grade C, no tariff line)
* IDB notification year 2025: a change of the tariff during 2025 (budget measures, stays of application) is not dated
* national import levies and charges outside the customs duty column (statistical, processing, ECOWAS/AU levies, import VAT advance) not modelled
* the price is taken before VAT and duty only: an excise inside the price needs "customsValue"
* lines left out (grade C): 10063020 (a preferential rate is specific or compound (not representable as a preference rate)); 10063080 (a preferential rate is specific or compound (not representable as a preference rate)); 17019910 (a preferential rate is specific or compound (not representable as a preference rate)); 17019920 (a preferential rate is specific or compound (not representable as a preference rate)); 17019990 (a preferential rate is specific or compound (not representable as a preference rate))
-/

